SUMMARY:Aug 28th Community Cuddles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your ticket\nhttps://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/aug-28-community-cuddl
 e\n\n**This is a non-sexual touch based event that invites participants to
  explore platonic intimacy in a safe environment** with like-minded people
 . We respect personal boundaries and through a supportive framework of mut
 ual agreements that maximize safety and create a space of easy openness an
 d compassionate connection.\nAt this event we have the chance to normalize
  touch with clear boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, consent-ba
 sed touch. We allow ourselves to be seen. We have fun.\nWe welcome people 
 of all backgrounds\, genders\, ethnicities\, relationship styles\, sexuali
 ties\, sizes\, and ages (18+).\n\n**THE RULES**\n1. Clothes stay on for th
 e whole event\\.\n2. You do not have to touch anyone at this event.\n3. Yo
 u must receive a verbal YES before you touch anyone.\n4. Take care of your
 self and those you choose to interact with.\n5. Speak up if you have a que
 stion\\\, concern\\\, or if you need assistance with anything during the e
 vent.\n6. All emotions are welcome\\- we love vulnerability.\n**WHY CUDDLE
 ?**\nTouch is a basic human need\, and many of us do not get enough\; most
  people don’t even know they are missing touch\, or have a way to ask fo
 r touch without sexualizing it. We believe deeply in the power of touch\, 
 and the importance of communication and consent in creating a safe space f
 or touch.\nCUDDLING WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers sounds weird o
 r scary to most people. “Will I like it?” “What if someone wants to 
 touch me and I don’t want to?” “What if I say yes and it’s not wha
 t I want?” “What if I really want to touch someone and they say no?”
  These are all normal questions. The answer is that this is a space create
 d to ask for exactly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you don’t want.
  Many people start out nervous at a cuddle event & most are really glad th
 ey came.\n\n**Schedule:**\n6:50-7pm: Arrive with snacks to share! Get comf
 ortable\, meet\, mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circle- its mandatory.
  We will set our container\, talk about personal boundaries\, communicatio
 n\, & consent.\n7:15pm: Icebreakers and connective activities.\n8:00pm: Op
 en cuddling! You MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ before touching or cu
 ddling with anybody at this event. If you are not sure how to do this – 
 great! – we will talk about it during the welcome circle.\n10:50pm: Clos
 ing Circle\, cleanup and head home.\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n*ARRIVE ON TIME: It 
 is important that all participants arrive before the Welcome Circle. The W
 elcome Circle serves the purpose of creating the safe space for consensual
 \, non-sexual touch between participants and making sure that everyone is 
 informed about consent.\n- Please arrive clean & as scent free as possible
 .\n*BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this event.\n\n**W
 HAT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to share\, a friend\, a d
 ate – whatever cuddle accessories you like! The only thing that you are 
 required to bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nThese events are not "gende
 r balanced".\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!** If you 
 experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to be 
 at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our best
  to create a safe environment which means that if someone is causing harm 
 (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm t
 hat takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and know
  that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n
 \n*refund policy-\nFull refund if you cancel 7 days before the event or yo
 u cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid/flu.\nCr
 edit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before an event
 .\nNo refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
