SUMMARY:Aug 29th An Evening of Spicy/Sensual Snuggles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your ticket-\nhttps://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/aug-29th-an-evening-o
 f-sensual-snuggles\n\nWhat is a Sensual Snuggle Event?**\nThis is a sweet 
 & welcoming event where we practice and use verbal consent to connect and 
 share touch. We talk about boundaries and practice both saying and receivi
 ng a “no”. In this space it is common to see people cuddle\, share mas
 sage\, have their hair brushed\, kiss\, expose nipples\, play\, laugh\, cr
 y\, and be vulnerable. This is a sober space where we can relax and connec
 t with other humans who are seeking touch based connection.\nWe strive for
  this to be a safe event. Safe touch enhances our ability to connect with 
 and trust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we are able to relax\
 , feel comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\n1- We ask for 
 what we want an wait for a yes before touching others.\n2- We say no if we
  don’t want to do something.\n3- We try to receive a no with grace and n
 ot take it personally.\n4- We arrive on time\, clean (as scent free as pos
 sible)\, and sober.\n5- We keep our pants/shorts on at this event. (Tops a
 re optional\; this is a sensual space\, not a sexual space.)\n6- We are he
 re to connect with others. Connection can be verbal\, platonic\, or spicy!
 \n7- We welcome diversity. Isms and Phobias are not welcome here!\n\n**Who
  should attend:**\nPeople who are interested in safely exploring touch and
  sensuality with strangers. This includes people who are single\, people w
 ho are not single\, couples\, folks who are new to town and looking for co
 nnection\, people of all/any genders and sexual orientations\, people of a
 ll ages (18 and up). People who understand and respect consent\, who will 
 take care of themselves and people around them. This event is queer-normat
 ive. The guest list will include all genders\, orientations\, ages\, and p
 ersonalities. If that’s not your thing… This is not the event for you.
 \n***Who should NOT attend:***\n-People who are only looking for a sex par
 ty.\n-People who do not understand and respect consent.\n-People who have 
 extreme fear of setting and speaking their personal boundaries\; in order 
 to create a safe space we need to know that you will say “no” if you f
 eel a no.\n-People who are homophobic\, racist\, sexist\, ageist\, ableist
 …\n-People under 18 years of age.\n***Schedule of the Evening***\n\n*6:5
 0pm Doors Open\, Mix & Mingle\n- 7:00pm We gather in a circle to meet each
  other\, build a container\, cover consent and boundary setting and discus
 s event agreements. Then we will play a few intimacy building games to mee
 t and connect with other people in the room. Please make sure you arrive o
 n-time!\n*8:15pm Once the container is built we will have self directed sn
 uggling and sensual interactions until the end of the party.\n- 10:50pm Cl
 osing Circle\; a time to re-center and connect as a group to verbally shar
 e anything that came up at the event or to voice gratitude to someone(s) y
 ou enjoyed interacting with.\n*11:00pm cleanup & head home\; you are welco
 me to help.\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!** If you e
 xperience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to be a
 t this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our best 
 to create a safe environment which means that if someone is causing harm (
 physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm th
 at takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and know 
 that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\
 nThese events are not "gender balanced"[. Check out our website for more i
 nformation about this decision.](http://holdmeavl.com/why-i-dont-gender-ba
 lance-events/)\n\n**Simple definitions/clarifications-** Platonic- marked 
 by the absence of romance or sex.\nMost of the interactions we have with f
 riends and strangers are platonic.\nSensual- gratification of the senses o
 r the indulgence of appetite.\nWe might feel sensual when we feel someone'
 s breath on our neck or experience a extra long and slow caress.\nSexual- 
 having or involving sex.\nOften involving one more more peoples genitals\;
  perhaps seeking orgasm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full refund if you cancel 7 da
 ys before the event or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct e
 xposure to covid. Credit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 
 days before an event. No refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event o
 r no-show.
